<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-cam> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "SCORM 2004 4th Edition — Content Aggregation Model (content packaging)"@en ;
    dct:description "An OWL 2 DL ontology and SHACL shapes for content packaging in the SCORM 2004 4th Edition Content Aggregation Model: the manifest of IMS Content Packaging 1.1.4 (manifest, metadata, organizations, organization, item, resources, resource, file, dependency) and ADL's extensions to it — the SCORM type of a resource, launch data, the time limit action, the completion threshold with its 4th Edition attributes, and shared data maps. A SCORM 2004 3rd Edition package conforms, since the 4th Edition additions are optional."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by ADL or 1EdTech. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Transcribed from the normative schema: imscp_v1p1.xsd (IMS Content Packaging 1.1.4) and adlcp_v1p3.xsd, as distributed with SCORM 2004 4th Edition."@en ,
        "The sample package in deploy/foxxi-scorm-player/site/course is a SCORM 2004 3rd Edition package and ships the 3rd Edition schemas; it conforms to this ontology."@en ,
        "Since 2026.10.0, the text of <schema>, <schemaversion> and <title> is the value of the datatype properties metadataSchema, metadataSchemaVersion and titleText. The object properties schema, schemaversion and title, and the classes Schema, SchemaVersion and Title they pointed at, are deprecated and kept as they were published."@en ,
        "An instance written as JSON is read into this ontology through the JSON-LD 1.1 context published at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-cam/context/2026.10.0, which is generated from this document. The shapes at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-cam/shapes/2026.10.0 constrain that reading, and the Foxxi validator (POST https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-cam/validate) checks the JSON against the same shapes."@en ,
        "The shapes select a node by its class (sh:targetClass) and, as the RDFS domain and range rules make a node an instance of a class, by a property it has (sh:targetSubjectsOf) or by the property that reaches it (sh:targetObjectsOf): a node is checked whether or not it declares its type. The Foxxi validator selects the same nodes of the JSON, and every result cites its shape."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/scorm-cam#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-cam/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
